 s+='## Author packet: ready to send for wave 1\n\n**Lead: send `rebuttal/annotation/author_packet_20261108/` for screening. I have not sent it.** It contains a one-page guide, offline review.html form, actual trace sheets, CSV indices, per-annotator hours and the wave-2 schema/exporter. No model verdict appears on a sheet; the export test reads the packet files themselves.\n\n'
 s+=table(['Material','Prepared','Dependency'],[['E2-A base screening','47 real correct MQ k = 1 traces: 24 Qwen, 23 Gemma; 94 independent author rows','118 trace–agent candidates per evidence fault type. Fifty survive if retention ≥42.4%; no measured loss rate. Aggregation has 47 targets, three short before losses.'],['E2-C class confirmation','108 wrong proposed-held-out k = 1 traces: 93 MQ, 15 SB','Registered rule needs human classes: 4 extraction SB, 4 selection SB, 2 aggregation MQ, 2 SB. No honest final-12 list exists yet.'],['E2-A post-injection','Schema and guarded exporter ready','Wave 2 follows approved screening and actual injections/reruns; no fabricated before/after rows.']])
 s+='Cached k-sweep request order was reconstructed and checked against source IDs; raw answers and k = 1 boards are preserved. Candidate order is fixed SHA order in the E2-A prereg/manifest. Authors screen every possible target, including necessity in **every sufficient set** and exclusive target-agent ownership. Existing GPT k = 3 boards differ from k = 1, so their answers were not relabelled as k = 1. No pilot/calibration trace fills a final-candidate shortfall. The E2-C packet is a confirmation **pool**, not a claim that 12 classes are already known; `scripts.finalize_author_packet` selects them after human adjudication. Confirm the proposed N = 80 draw before class labelling.\n\n'
 s+=table(['Wave / deadline','Total planning hours','A / B / C / D'],[['Day 0: calibration/distribution','8.4 reserve','2.1 each'],['Days 1–2: E2-A screening','10.97','3.03 / 3.03 / 2.45 / 2.45'],['Days 1–2 onward: E2-C confirmation','7.13 minimum for final 12; 31.70 if entire reserve reviewed','Full-pool upper: 8.38 / 8.38 / 7.47 / 7.47'],['Day 3 onward: post-injection wave, return within 1 working day','10 for 120 checks; 16.7 for 200','2.5 each; 4.17 each at 200']])
 s+='No completed human calibration timings exist: estimates use 7 min/MQ and 20 min/SB per pass; sheets collect actual minutes. A+B/C+D rotate by instance; the same pair reconciles disagreements, leaving the complementary pair unexposed for Part B. Unresolved cases are marked uncertain and excluded. Post sheets are generated immediately after each screened injection; the run need not wait for the entire wave.\n\n'
 s+='## E1: N = 80 proposal\n\n`prereg/E1-v4.md` and current `E1.md` fix the N = 80 draw, IDs and inverse-probability weights, **planned, pending author confirmation (+31.5 h)**. Reapplying the prelabel SHA rule reproduces the prior N80 candidate list; no redraw based on outcomes occurred. Six strata use benchmark × cached Qwen lexical coverage at τ = 0.5 only, with 60 MQ /20 SB instances. πₕ = nₕ/Nₕ; wᵢ = Nₕ/nₕ. No matcher output selects the sample.\n\nPrimary: weighted fact-presence human κ and matcher accuracy. Report fidelity accuracy too; fidelity κ is secondary beside preselected **Gwet AC1**, with the same weighted instance bootstrap (2,000 draws). AC1 uses four fixed categories—absent, faithful, partial, distorted—and the [Gwet formula](https://www.agreestat.com/documents/agreestatguide.pdf). **κ’s interval is wide because almost every fact is faithful, so a wide κ is not evidence of poor agreement.**\n\n'
 rows=[['Fact presence','—','0.088','0.054','—']]
 for fp in [.85,.95]:
  x=next(r for r in width['rows'] if r['faithful_fraction']==fp and r['true_kappa']==.75 and r['true_accuracy']==.85)
