 s+=table(['Experiment','Benchmark','R1 backbone','Primary code-only invalid','Strict sensitivity invalid'],rows)
 s+=table(['E2-A R1 technical family attribution','Primary code-only','Strict sensitivity'],[[r['setting'][1].split('/')[-1],f"{r['primary_scores']['family']}/{r['n']}",f"{r['sensitivity_scores']['family']}/{r['n']}"] for r in scores['settings'] if 'primary_scores' in r])
 s+='**The ordering reverses:** strict favours Qwen (3/10 vs 2/10); the released primary favours Gemini (4/10 vs 3/10). These are technical items, including unkept cases, not human-validated efficacy estimates. E2-C has no human references yet. Every future E2/E2-C result table must show both scorings and invalid rates.\n\n'
 s+='All 16 strict-invalid relay outputs omit only the mode name; agent/step/code are valid. W&W step-by-step abstains 7/20 (Qwen 3/10, Gemini 4/10); it is not a malformed-output problem. Transcript-token quartiles show no consistent length trend; numbering/names are valid and no input is empty. The same name omission occurs on 1/5 own R1 examples. No input fault was established, so no renderer change or extra paid baseline calls were made.\n\n'
